+
+## Decisions & Alternatives
+
+| Decision | Chosen | Rationale |
+|---|---|---|
+| Lookup backend | Local embedded SQLite index, rebuilt from each signed snapshot | Kiosks have no runtime network route (HLD tenet) and receive updates only via signed USB snapshots (HLD tenet), so the backend has to work fully offline and rebuild from a file each kiosk already validates. A local index needs no service to run and keeps index maintenance inside this node, at the cost of each kiosk validating and rebuilding its own index per snapshot. |
+| Considered: on-site HTTPS directory | Rejected | One centrally maintained index and smaller kiosk updates, but registry lookups would depend on the lab network and need service-timeout handling — kiosks have no network route during normal operation, so this was never viable under the current HLD tenets. |
+| Considered: managed search service | Rejected | Less index maintenance and room for richer search later, but recurring cost, credentials, and external connectivity are all excluded by the kiosk's isolated, offline operating mode. |
